1
00:03:32,571 --> 00:03:38,571
The Star Wars saga continues.

2
00:07:05,142 --> 00:07:11,142
The Empire Strikes Back is a adventure, action, science
fiction film directed by Irvin Kershner.

3
00:10:37,714 --> 00:10:43,714
The epic saga continues as Luke Skywalker, in hopes of defeating the evil
Galactic Empire, learns the ways of the Jedi from aging master Yoda.

4
00:14:10,285 --> 00:14:16,285
But Darth Vader is more determined than ever to capture Luke.

5
00:17:42,857 --> 00:17:48,857
Meanwhile, rebel leader Princess Leia, cocky Han Solo, Chewbacca, and droids C-3PO and
R2-D2 are thrown into various stages of capture, betrayal and despair.

6
00:21:15,428 --> 00:21:21,428
Luke Skywalker, played by Mark Hamill.

7
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:54,000
Han Solo, played by Harrison Ford.

8
00:28:20,571 --> 00:28:26,571
Princess Leia, played by Carrie Fisher.

9
00:31:53,142 --> 00:31:59,142
Lando Calrissian, played by Billy Dee Williams.

10
00:35:25,714 --> 00:35:31,714
C-3PO, played by Anthony Daniels.

11
00:38:58,285 --> 00:39:04,285
Darth Vader, played by David Prowse.

12
00:42:30,857 --> 00:42:36,857
The Empire Strikes Back (also known as Star Wars: Episode V – The Empire Strikes Back) is a 1980 American epic space opera film
directed by Irvin Kershner from a screenplay by Leigh Brackett and Lawrence Kasdan, based on a story by George Lucas.

13
00:46:03,428 --> 00:46:09,428
The sequel to Star Wars (1977), it is the second film in the Star Wars film
series and the fifth chronological chapter of the "Skywalker Saga".

14
00:49:36,000 --> 00:49:42,000
Set three years after the events of Star Wars, the film recounts the battle between the malevolent Galactic
Empire, led by the Emperor, and the Rebel Alliance, led by Luke Skywalker and Princess Leia.

15
00:53:08,571 --> 00:53:14,571
As the Empire goes on the offensive, Luke trains to master the Force so he
can confront the Emperor's powerful disciple, Darth Vader.

16
00:56:41,142 --> 00:56:47,142
The ensemble cast includes Mark Hamill, Harrison Ford, Carrie Fisher, Billy Dee Williams,
Anthony Daniels, David Prowse, Kenny Baker, Peter Mayhew, and Frank Oz.

17
01:00:13,714 --> 01:00:19,714
Following the success of Star Wars, Lucas hired Brackett to write the sequel.

18
01:03:46,285 --> 01:03:52,285
After she died in 1978, he outlined the entire Star Wars saga and wrote the next draft himself,
before hiring Raiders of the Lost Ark (1981) writer Kasdan to enhance his work.

19
01:07:18,857 --> 01:07:24,857
To avoid the stress he faced directing Star Wars, Lucas handed the responsibility to Kershner and
focused on expanding his special effects company Industrial Light & Magic instead.

20
01:10:51,428 --> 01:10:57,428
Filmed from March to September 1979 in Finse, Norway, and at Elstree Studios in England, The Empire Strikes Back faced production
difficulties, including actor injuries, illnesses, fires, and problems securing additional financing as costs rose.

21
01:14:24,000 --> 01:14:30,000
Initially budgeted at $8 million, costs had risen to
$30.5 million by the project's conclusion.

22
01:17:56,571 --> 01:18:02,571
Released by Twentieth Century-Fox on May 21, 1980, the highly anticipated sequel became the
highest-grossing film that year, earning approximately $401.5 million worldwide.

23
01:21:29,142 --> 01:21:35,142
Unlike its lighthearted predecessor, Empire met with mixed reviews from critics,
and fans were conflicted about its darker and more mature themes.

24
01:25:01,714 --> 01:25:07,714
The film was nominated for various awards and won two Academy
Awards, two Grammy Awards, and a BAFTA, among others.

25
01:28:34,285 --> 01:28:40,285
Subsequent releases have raised the film's worldwide gross to $549–$550 million and, adjusted for
inflation, it is the 13th-highest-grossing film in the United States and Canada.

26
01:32:06,857 --> 01:32:12,857
Since its release, The Empire Strikes Back has been critically reassessed and is now often regarded
as the best film in the Star Wars series and among the greatest films ever made.

27
01:35:39,428 --> 01:35:45,428
It has had a significant influence on filmmaking and popular culture and is often
considered an example of a sequel superior to its predecessor.

28
01:39:12,000 --> 01:39:18,000
The climax, in which Darth Vader reveals he is Luke's father, is often
ranked as one of the greatest plot twists in cinema.

29
01:42:44,571 --> 01:42:50,571
The film spawned a variety of merchandise and adaptations,
including video games and a radio play.

30
01:46:17,142 --> 01:46:23,142
The United States Library of Congress selected it for
preservation in the National Film Registry in 2010.

31
01:49:49,714 --> 01:49:55,714
Return of the Jedi (1983) followed Empire,
concluding the original Star Wars trilogy.

32
01:53:22,285 --> 01:53:28,285
Prequel and sequel trilogies have since been released.

33
01:56:54,857 --> 01:57:00,857
The film explores themes of rebellion, android, spacecraft, asteroid, rebel.

34
02:00:27,428 --> 02:00:33,428
The tone is thought_provoking.
